WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions of "Citric Acid Cycle" by Drew Berry, wehi.tv, for HHMI BioInteractive, from the film's page on YouTube (youtu.be/IlSFn0gRyC4).
Each cue is one line here, and mishearings in the captions are put right (plans/follow-the-molecule/captions.py lists them).

1
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:05.310
The origin of energy production and biosynthesis

2
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:12.390
inside your living cells is the dynamic mitochondria organelle.

3
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.410
Mitochondria are filled with metabolic enzymes that

4
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.410
catalyze a loop of chemical reactions

5
00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.640
called the citric acid cycle.

6
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.870
The eight steps of the citric acid cycle

7
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:30.740
gradually break apart two carbon atoms from glycolysis,

8
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.220
capturing liberated electrons for the electron transport

9
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.360
chain, while generating carbon dioxide as waste.

10
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.640
The citric acid cycle starts with the end product

11
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.150
of a previous cycle, the four carbon molecule oxaloacetate.

12
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.670
New carbon enters from glycolysis

13
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.030
in the form of acetyl CoA, a two carbon acetyl

14
00:00:55.030 --> 00:01:00.150
group attached to coenzyme A.

15
00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:04.680
Step 1 is the catalytic transfer of a two carbon acetyl

16
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.270
group from coenzyme A to four carbon oxaloacetate,

17
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:12.780
creating six carbon citric acid, the molecule that

18
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.250
gives the cycle its name.

19
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.000
Citric acid is used by your cells

20
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.440
for the biosynthesis of fatty acids, lipids, and cholesterol,

21
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.945
and is also the substrate for step 2 of the citric acid

22
00:01:27.945 --> 00:01:28.445
cycle.

23
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.650
The enzyme reaction of step 2 makes a small change

24
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.930
to the citric acid molecule, moving

25
00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.350
the position of an oxygen atom, converting citrate

26
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.520
into isocitrate.

27
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.440
Step 3 of this cycle removes the carbon atom,

28
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.760
forming carbon dioxide as waste, while converting six carbon

29
00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.506
isocitrate to five carbon ketoglutarate.

30
00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.310
During this process, chemical energy

31
00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:11.400
is harvested when two electrons are transferred

32
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.910
to coenzyme NADH, which delivers them

33
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:18.210
to nearby enzymes of the electron transport chain.

34
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.900
Step 4 of the citric acid cycle is

35
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.680
performed by a huge multi-enzyme complex,

36
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.170
connecting multiple chemical reactions

37
00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.480
with flexible tethers, efficiently

38
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.480
moving reactants between active sites

39
00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.830
and diverting electrons between pathways.

40
00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:45.270
The large complex is made with a repeating unit of three core

41
00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.720
enzymes working in sequence to remove a carbon

42
00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.830
atom from ketoglutarate, generating carbon dioxide

43
00:02:52.830 --> 00:03:07.450
waste, then attaching four carbon succinyl to coenzyme A.

44
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.600
The electron from ketoglutarate oxidation

45
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.150
is retained by the tethered enzyme

46
00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:18.760
before passing it to coenzyme NADH, which delivers electrons

47
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.710
to the electron transport chain.

48
00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.710
Enzymes of step 5 separate succinyl from coenzyme A

49
00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:52.580
by breaking an energetic bond, providing enough energy

50
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.400
to create GTP.

51
00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:00.320
GTP is a building block of RNA and an energy source

52
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.750
for protein synthesis.

53
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:07.860
In the most direct path to ATP from the citric acid cycle,

54
00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.280
other enzymes in the matrix can use GTP

55
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.425
to make the chemical fuel ATP.

56
00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.820
Step 6 is performed by an enzyme embedded

57
00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.700
in the inner mitochondrial membrane.

58
00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.660
This enzyme is also known as complex two of the electron

59
00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.610
transport chain.

60
00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.620
The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of succinate

61
00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.980
to create fumarate, releasing two electrons

62
00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.745
that hop through the interior to coenzyme Q, which is reduced.

63
00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:50.960
Coenzyme Q travels in the membrane carrying the electrons

64
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.140
to nearby enzymes of the electron transport chain.

65
00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.240
Step 7 takes fumarate generated by step 6

66
00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.255
and reacts it with water to create four carbon malate.

67
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.790
The final step of the citric acid cycle

68
00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:24.240
uses malate to regenerate oxaloacetate,

69
00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.860
transferring electrons to coenzyme NADH, which supplies

70
00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.930
the electron transport chain.

71
00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.750
Oxaloacetate can return to step 1 for another loop of the cycle

72
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.460
and is also an essential building

73
00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:43.740
block for making amino acids and the genetic code of DNA

74
00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:44.265
and RNA.

75
00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.140
At the center of cellular metabolism,

76
00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:54.040
the citric acid cycle generates both chemical energy

77
00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:58.030
and material for biosynthesis of the entire diversity

78
00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:02.370
of molecules found inside a living cell.
